From: mscharged-port
Subject: Reuse staged index lists
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance. Apply after 0127.

The parser turns every quad, strip and fan draw into a triangle index list
relative to the draw's own vertices, so the list depends only on the
primitive and the vertex count; it rebuilt and staged it for every draw (the
largest single cost of the FIFO consumer). The lists already staged in the
current packet are now kept, and a draw with the same primitive and vertex
count points at the same bytes; a new list is written straight into the
staging region by a plain loop (checked equal to prepare_idx_buffer for
every primitive and 33408 vertex counts, including its 16-bit count). A draw
whose list does not end the index region stays unmerged: the same triangles
in the same order.

